course: dictionary
lesson: 6576
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nightmare can be a frightening or very upsetting dream. «Nightmares are common in children, and are often linked to stress or scary stories.» The clue is that nightmares happen when you are asleep, so this is the dream meaning.
explain: A nightmare can also be a very difficult or unpleasant situation. «My dad's a nightmare anyway» does not mean he is a dream. The word anyway and the rude, grumpy tone show that he is hard to be around.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: does the sentence talk about sleep or dreams? If it does, use the dream meaning. If not, try the other meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A nightmare is a frightening or very upsetting dream.
fact: A nightmare can also be a very difficult or unpleasant situation or experience.
fact: «Nightmares can feel very real, but they are only dreams and cannot hurt you.»
fact: Nightmares after a scary film are common, and they usually fade after a few nights.
fact: Phrases to know: «have a nightmare», «wake up from a nightmare», «a nightmare journey», «a living nightmare».
exercise: «Nightmares after a scary film are common; they fade after a few nights.» What does nightmare mean here? | A very difficult journey | *A frightening, upsetting dream | A pleasant song | A calm bedtime
exercise: «The traffic jam on the motorway was a nightmare, and we were late for the party.» What does nightmare mean here? | A frightening dream | A quiet, calm evening | *A very difficult, unpleasant situation
exercise: «Nightmares can feel very real, but they are only dreams and cannot hurt you.» What does «cannot hurt you» tell you about a nightmare? | It is very loud | It will always come true | It is a kind of food | *It cannot harm you
test: «My dad's a nightmare anyway, you're not missing much.» What does nightmare mean in this sentence? | A frightening dream | *Someone very difficult or unpleasant to be around | A nightlight | A scary film
test: «Wake up from a nightmare» means: | Wake up in a new house | Wake up late for school | *Wake up from a frightening dream | Go back to sleep and forget everything
exam: Which sentence uses nightmare in the second meaning? | «Turn on a light if you wake up from a bad dream.» | «I had a nightmare about spiders last night.» | *«The bus broke down, so the trip home was a nightmare.» | «Nightmares are common in children.»
